From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:33:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] prime, lazarus-gateway: find gateways that can't carry
 NTA attestations before activation

Stock datum_gateway v0.4.1 stops reading a coinbaser at the first script over
64 bytes (datum_coinbaser.c:795) and says nothing, so after XBT-NTA activation
it would keep the payees, drop the 70-byte attestations and mine bad-nta-count
blocks (SOV-007). SOV-011:

- Capability flag: a gateway that keeps 70-byte outputs sends "nta-v1\0" in
  its hello right after the header key seed, where stock sends one rand()
  byte repeated (datum_protocol.c:1028-1033) that every server skips.
  lazarus-gateway and the split-only C patch send it.
- Probe: from nta-height - nta-probe-window (2016), one coinbaser per
  non-advertising gateway per nta-probe-every-secs (3600) ends with a
  zero-value 70-byte NTA-shaped OP_RETURN. The first full-split share on it
  decides: kept, ready; dropped, nta-unready. It pays nobody and share
  classification skips zero-value OP_RETURNs, so payouts do not change.
  After activation the attestations themselves are the probe.
- Policy (nta-unready-policy): refuse (default) sends a DATUM server
  message (proto cmd 7, logged at INFO by stock) and mining sub-command
  0x4e (unknown to stock, logged at WARN "Perhaps you need to upgrade"),
  then closes. An upgraded gateway that advertises is served at once.
  pool-only serves pool-only coinbasers and says why that cannot work: the
  pool's own output needs its 70-byte attestation too.
- /nta.json "readiness": gateways and share of the last hour's work that
  are ready / nta-unready / unknown, and blocks until activation.
- datum_wire::coinbaser::stock_v041_parse, and lazarus-gateway's
  LAZARUS_GATEWAY_EMULATE_STOCK_V041=1 demo hook, play stock's parser.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
